cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
title: "desktop-control-verify: cached-element control of Windows desktop applications, drawing-to-specification extraction and code-enforced build verification"
abstract: >-
  General-purpose layers extracted, with their development history, from a private
  system that automates design entry in a Windows cabinet-design application that has no
  automation interface. The control layer discovers the application's UI Automation tree
  once and then drives it through cached, window-relative element positions. The
  verification layer compares a vision-model extraction of a drawing with independent
  readings of the drawing and of the built result, and decides PASS or FAIL in code.
  The underlying development took place privately between January and March 2026.
authors:
